From badf00aafd64d770d2d8fcb4ab21032e127a5181 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haribabu Krishnasamy <hkr@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Dec 2025 12:51:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM:PROTOCOL:HOSTAPD: Move supported/basic
rates configuration from radio level to BSS level

Hostapd currently handles supported and basic rate sets at the radio/interface level,
causing all BSSs on the same interface to share the same configuration. This prevents
per‑BSS customization of rate advertising and enforcement.

This change moves supported_rates and basic_rates from the global hostapd_config
into hostapd_bss_config and prepares filtered, per‑BSS rate tables in hapd.
The per‑BSS rates are then used when constructing beacons and probe responses,
when initializing station defaults, and when reporting via ctrl_iface status.
AP/mesh paths in wpa_supplicant are updated to set BSS‑level rate arrays,
and memory management is adjusted accordingly to avoid iface‑level storage.

If a BSS does not explicitly configure basic_rates, sane defaults are chosen based
on the current HW mode (11a/11b/11g). For 11ad, no basic rates are used.

Patch-dependency: None

Signed-off-by: Haribabu Krishnasamy <hkr@qti.qualcomm.com>
